// Reuse schedule: single host, `reuse` hint on the inner x-loop.
//
// TASK-0265 Stage 2 (this cycle): a single-`host` variant that carries
// the reuse loop directive WITHOUT any partition= or async transfer
// machinery. Lets reuse Stage 2 wiring (TASK-0265) make its first
// landing on a clean cell — no halo/partition/transfer entanglement,
// no async/buffer/notify capability matrix, and no skip-list cells.
//
// The original `reuse` use site is `05-stencil/distributed`'s
// `loop x : block=64, vectorize=8, reuse;` — but that cell is
// currently SKIPPED on every backend due to TASK-0267 (host-Push drop
// under partitioned consumers + async transfer) and TASK-0268
// (sync_inject barrier deadlock on unequal-iter partitioned bodies),
// neither of which has any relation to reuse codegen. This single-host
// schedule isolates the reuse hint so its codegen can be exercised
// e2e independently.
//
// What reuse_inference Stage 1 (TASK-0261) records for THIS schedule:
//   For the inner `for x : 1..W-1` loop body, `blur3` reads
//   `img_in[y±1][x-1]`, `img_in[y±1][x]`, `img_in[y±1][x+1]` — the
//   axis-1 (x) offset set is {-1, 0, +1} on `img_in`. With
//   `loop x : reuse;` in scope, the inference pass writes:
//
//     ACFG::reuse_widths[x_iv][img_in_id][1] =
//         ReuseSlot { min_offset: -1, length: 3 }
//
//   The y-axis (axis 0) carries offsets {-1, 0, +1} too but `y` does
//   not carry `reuse`, so no entry is recorded under y_iv.
//
// What Stage 2 (this task) wires:
//   At loop-entry of the `x` `Event::Loop`, the backend walker reads
//   `sidecar.reuse_widths.get(x_iv)` and either (a) emits a
//   circular-buffer prologue + per-iteration rewrite of every
//   `img_in[y][x+b]` read inside the body, or (b) emits a `//` comment
//   marker line per (data, axis, ReuseSlot) at body-entry naming the
//   would-be buffer slot (Tier 1 of TASK-0265 — keeps emitted bytes
//   byte-identical to non-reuse blocked baseline because a Rust comment
//   carries no runtime semantics; Stage 2 real circular-buffer emit
//   forward-carried to TASK-0269/0270).
//
// E2E expectation:
//   - Tier 1 (marker-comment only): cell PASS, bit-identical to a
//     `loop x : block=N;` baseline (no reuse). The marker substring
//     `reuse_widths_pending` is grep-able in the emitted main.rs.
//   - Tier 2/3 (real buffer emit, TASK-0269/0270): cell PASS, still
//     bit-identical to `reference.bin` (reuse is a perf rewrite, not a
//     semantic one). Emitted code contains a 'reuse_buf' / 'circular'
//     marker that the test crate can grep for.

schedule for "../prog.algo.nuc" {
    workers = { host };

    place load_image on host;
    place save_image on host;
    place blur3      on host;

    // No block= on y — reuse is the only loop-option this schedule
    // exercises, so the cell isolates the reuse codegen path without
    // strip-mine confound.
    //
    // Inner x-loop carries the `reuse` hint. Stage 1 (TASK-0261)
    // populates the reuse_widths sidecar; Stage 2 (TASK-0265) is the
    // consumer.
    loop x : reuse;
}
